# Keep JavaScript at LF in the working tree as well as in the repository.
#
# core.autocrlf is true and there was no .gitattributes, so every blob is stored
# LF but checkout rewrote scripts to CRLF. Deploys copy from the working tree,
# which meant the bytes landing on a site depended on whether git had touched the
# file since the last deploy rather than on its content: js/courtroom.js went out
# LF, then a branch checkout flipped the working copy to CRLF and the same code
# started reading as a difference against both sites.
#
# text keeps the index normalised to LF, so diffs are unaffected; eol=lf makes
# checkout agree with it.
*.js text eol=lf
